1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,520
One hundred squats.

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:02,510
Every day.

3
00:00:02,890 --> 00:00:03,780
For thirty days.

4
00:00:04,159 --> 00:00:06,589
No gym, no weights, just my legs.

5
00:00:06,989 --> 00:00:09,070
That's three thousand squats!

6
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:10,720
Your knees are going to file a

7
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,530
complaint.

8
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:13,089
That's what I thought too.

9
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,220
But on day ten, something happened that

10
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,169
I didn't expect.

11
00:00:16,549 --> 00:00:17,379
Stay for that one.

12
00:00:17,779 --> 00:00:18,329
Day one.

13
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:20,410
I did them in sets of twenty-five.

14
00:00:20,789 --> 00:00:22,230
By the last set, my legs were

15
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,410
shaking like jelly.

16
00:00:23,809 --> 00:00:25,539
The next morning, I couldn't sit down

17
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:26,589
without holding the wall.

18
00:00:26,989 --> 00:00:28,000
And the stairs?

19
00:00:28,139 --> 00:00:29,250
How were the stairs?

20
00:00:29,649 --> 00:00:31,239
Going down the stairs was the worst

21
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:31,609
part.

22
00:00:31,989 --> 00:00:33,200
That's normal soreness.

23
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:35,520
Your muscles get tiny damage, then they

24
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,080
repair and come back stronger.

25
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:38,039
Day five.

26
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,469
The soreness was gone.

27
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:41,570
One hundred squats took me just eight

28
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:42,080
minutes.

29
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,609
Here's why it works.

30
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:45,840
A squat uses the biggest muscles in

31
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:46,370
your body.

32
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,740
Your thighs, your glutes, and your core

33
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:49,750
all work together.

34
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,370
So it's leg day.

35
00:00:51,490 --> 00:00:52,390
Every day.

36
00:00:52,789 --> 00:00:53,469
Exactly.

37
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:54,490
Day ten.

38
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:55,900
Here's the surprise.

39
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,870
My knees used to crack and ache

40
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:58,570
on the stairs.

41
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,929
Now they felt better, not worse.

42
00:01:01,330 --> 00:01:03,400
Strong thigh muscles take pressure off your

43
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:03,810
knees.

44
00:01:04,170 --> 00:01:06,159
Squats done right don't wreck your knees.

45
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:07,129
They protect them.

46
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:09,129
Just keep your heels down, and let

47
00:01:09,129 --> 00:01:10,609
your knees point the same way as

48
00:01:10,609 --> 00:01:11,170
your toes.

49
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:12,109
Day twenty.

50
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:14,359
My jeans felt tight around my thighs.

51
00:01:14,590 --> 00:01:15,200
In a good way.

52
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:15,969
Wait.

53
00:01:15,969 --> 00:01:18,060
Your legs got bigger without weights?

54
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:19,439
A little, yes.

55
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:21,379
For a beginner, one hundred reps a

56
00:01:21,379 --> 00:01:22,579
day is enough to grow.

57
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,680
And my glutes finally filled out my

58
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:25,170
pants.

59
00:01:25,570 --> 00:01:27,030
Too much information.

60
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:28,030
Day thirty.

61
00:01:28,370 --> 00:01:29,240
The final test.

62
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,329
On day one, I could do thirty-five

63
00:01:31,329 --> 00:01:32,409
squats without stopping.

64
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:34,159
Today, I did one hundred in a

65
00:01:34,159 --> 00:01:34,530
row.

66
00:01:34,930 --> 00:01:36,659
Almost three times more.

67
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,490
My legs look stronger, stairs feel easy,

68
00:01:39,689 --> 00:01:40,740
and I can stand up from the

69
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:41,850
floor without hands.

70
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:44,150
The sit-down stand-up test!

71
00:01:44,150 --> 00:01:45,299
Ten points!

72
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:46,390
Ten points.

73
00:01:46,390 --> 00:01:48,000
But here's the honest part.

74
00:01:48,379 --> 00:01:49,930
After two weeks, it got easy.

75
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:51,510
To keep growing, you have to make

76
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:51,990
it harder.

77
00:01:52,390 --> 00:01:54,219
Slow down each rep, pause at the

78
00:01:54,219 --> 00:01:56,000
bottom, or hold a backpack full of

79
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:56,420
books.

80
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,049
If you want to try it, start

81
00:01:58,049 --> 00:01:59,920
with fifty a day, in small sets.

82
00:02:00,299 --> 00:02:01,829
Add ten more every few days.

83
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,519
Feet shoulder width apart.

84
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,269
Sit back like there's a chair behind

85
00:02:05,269 --> 00:02:05,439
you.

86
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:06,320
Chest up.

87
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:07,790
Then push through your heels.

88
00:02:08,189 --> 00:02:09,379
How many squats can you do in

89
00:02:09,379 --> 00:02:10,180
a row right now?

90
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:12,050
Test it, and comment your number.
